{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019is2uhWdtjiDw3B88g2ue7","type":"tool_result","content":"585\t\n586\t---\n587\t\n588\t## Rule 6 — canon conflicts carried into Chapter 4's shards\n589\t\n590\tNo shard was overwritten (none of the ten existed). Conflicts recorded loudly inside the\n591\tshards that later chapters will read:\n592\t\n593\t1. **`Lease` ownership** — three-way, settled by B2 in Chapter 8's favor. Evidence line\n594\t   quoted in `concepts/namespace.md` so Chapter 5's and Chapter 12's Stage 14 do not\n595\t   re-litigate it.\n596\t2. **Convention 5 broken.** Chapter 3's ledger proposed *\"No `§N` in cross-bearings that\n597\t   point into undrafted chapters\"* and followed it 18 times out of 20. Chapter 4 pins\n598\t   §-numbers into **eleven** undrafted chapters, **fifteen** times. Never ratified, so this\n599\t   is a governance call rather than a defect — but it is the direct cause of item 3.\n600\t3. **§N reservation register — now three-deep on two targets.** Recorded in\n601\t   `concepts/cluster-scoped-resource.md` (which carries the Ch 12 bearings) and\n602\t   `concepts/label-selector.md` (which carries the Ch 6 and Ch 9 ones):\n603\t\n604\t   | Target | Claimed by | For |\n605\t   |---|---|---|\n606\t   | **Ch 12 §2** | ch 2 (L393) / ch 4 | signing & attestation · why RBAC names subjects instead of selecting them |\n607\t   | **Ch 12 §3** | ch 2 (L459) / ch 4 | restricting who can pull what · deriving Role/ClusterRole/RoleBinding/ClusterRoleBinding |\n608\t   | **Ch 12 §4** | ch 2 (L813) / ch 4 | runtime protection for compute · hardening Secrets |\n609\t   | **Ch 6 §3** | ch 1 (L435) / ch 2 (L600) / ch 4 | StatefulSets · CRDs · a controller's selector and the Pods it owns |\n610\t   | **Ch 9 §4** | ch 2 (L871) / ch 4 | NetworkPolicy · cluster DNS and FQDNs — **Ch 4 is right; B2 row 10 puts NetworkPolicy in Ch 10** |\n611\t\n612\t   Cheapest resolution consistent with the proposed convention: demote Chapter 4's forward\n613\t   bearings to bare `Ch N` and let each target chapter's outline assign its own numbers.\n614\t   That also stops Chapter 5 from adding a fourth claim to `Ch 6 §3`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7eee19e-037a-467d-aefb-84c30699c926","uuid":"ebebb9f7-97ac-45c4-a5b9-18de00f4b867","timestamp":"2026-08-25T00:26:00.522Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-04\\kb-manifest.md","content":"\n---\n\n## Rule 6 — canon conflicts carried into Chapter 4's shards\n\nNo shard was overwritten (none of the ten existed). Conflicts recorded loudly inside the\nshards that later chapters will read:\n\n1. **`Lease` ownership** — three-way, settled by B2 in Chapter 8's favor. Evidence line\n   quoted in `concepts/namespace.md` so Chapter 5's and Chapter 12's Stage 14 do not\n   re-litigate it.\n2. **Convention 5 broken.** Chapter 3's ledger proposed *\"No `§N` in cross-bearings that\n   point into undrafted chapters\"* and followed it 18 times out of 20. Chapter 4 pins\n   §-numbers into **eleven** undrafted chapters, **fifteen** times. Never ratified, so this\n   is a governance call rather than a defect — but it is the direct cause of item 3.\n3. **§N reservation register — now three-deep on two targets.** Recorded in\n   `concepts/cluster-scoped-resource.md` (which carries the Ch 12 bearings) and\n   `concepts/label-selector.md` (which carries the Ch 6 and Ch 9 ones):\n\n   | Target | Claimed by | For |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | **Ch 12 §2** | ch 2 (L393) / ch 4 | signing & attestation · why RBAC names subjects instead of selecting them |\n   | **Ch 12 §3** | ch 2 (L459) / ch 4 | restricting who can pull what · deriving Role/ClusterRole/RoleBinding/ClusterRoleBinding |\n   | **Ch 12 §4** | ch 2 (L813) / ch 4 | runtime protection for compute · hardening Secrets |\n   | **Ch 6 §3** | ch 1 (L435) / ch 2 (L600) / ch 4 | StatefulSets · CRDs · a controller's selector and the Pods it owns |\n   | **Ch 9 §4** | ch 2 (L871) / ch 4 | NetworkPolicy · cluster DNS and FQDNs — **Ch 4 is right; B2 row 10 puts NetworkPolicy in Ch 10** |\n\n   Cheapest resolution consistent with the proposed convention: demote Chapter 4's forward\n   bearings to bare `Ch N` and let each target chapter's outline assign its own numbers.\n   That also stops Chapter 5 from adding a fourth claim to `Ch 6 §3`.","numLines":30,"startLine":585,"totalLines":1658}}}
